      "problem": "Find the **polar** coordinates of the point where the polar curve $r=3.5$ intersects the positive $y$-axis.",
      "worked_solution": "The polar curve $r=3.5$ is a circle of radius $3.5$ centered at the origin. It crosses the positive $y$-axis at the point where $r=3.5$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13959689/assets/dc12f535f40d75a21fc367bf6e08cde9f4ec086c4f358e4ab198a6f44da1aac4.png)\n\nTherefore, the point of intersection in polar coordinates is $(3.5,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$",
